WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.220 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the mountains of northern Yemen, little Shlomo grew up
beside his father, Zechariah.

2
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.140 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
His father died when Shlomo was about three.

3
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.980 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The study house..... A few years later.

4
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.850 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“There were four of us children to one book.”

5
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.730 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“And this way we could read the book…”

6
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.410 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the front or the back, from the right or the left.

7
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.320 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We could read it.”

8
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.970 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
As a boy, he also learned a trade.

9
00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.800 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We worked as blacksmiths.”

10
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:47.050 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In the workshop they shaped iron and learned to guide each
hammer blow.

11
00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:52.840 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Kadia, Shlomo’s mother
“And my mother, I was maybe fifteen …”

12
00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:54.400 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“She died.”

13
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.620 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After his mother died, Shlomo went to live with his aunt
Badra. She was the sister of his father, Zechariah.

14
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.390 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“There was my father’s sister …”

15
00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.320 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“Badra.”

16
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.690 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
While still in Saada, Shlomo wanted to move to the Land of
Israel.

17
00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:22.500 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
He recalled setting out for Aden at nineteen to seek an
immigration permit.

18
00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:28.030 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo set off on foot, leaving the stone houses of the
mountains behind.

19
00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.030 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“On donkeys.”

20
00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.450 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“It took us about two weeks.”

21
00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:39.450 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From place to place. We walk by day …”

22
00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:41.750 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“… and at night we sleep.”

23
00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:56.400 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From the mountains around Saada, the caravan headed south.

24
00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:02.030 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Roughly 600–700 km. He recalled about two weeks on foot
and with donkeys.

25
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:06.310 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Aden, the roles were reversed.

26
00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.110 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“I had pupils there. I used to teach them.”

27
00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:15.030 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“And I received a salary.”

28
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:22.300 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The boy who had studied so diligently was now a teacher
himself.

29
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:30.350 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Aden, Shlomo went to see the official in charge of
immigration.

30
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:35.140 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“How old are you? I told them twenty-five.”

31
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.060 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
He remembered being twenty at the time.

32
00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.270 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“In the end they approved my aliyah.”

33
00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.820 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
About a year later came the day of departure.

34
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.290 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From Aden we went by ship.”

35
00:02:51.207 --> 00:02:56.137 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Until now, the journey was measured in footsteps. From
here, the sea would carry Shlomo.

36
00:02:56.287 --> 00:03:00.905 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
The ship sailed north through the Red Sea to the Suez
Canal.

37
00:03:02.065 --> 00:03:05.932 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“We stayed in Port Said for one day.”

38
00:03:07.832 --> 00:03:14.682 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
“From there they sent us a car from the Land of Israel.”

39
00:03:14.942 --> 00:03:19.238 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Beyond the canal, the road turned northeast toward Tel
Aviv.

40
00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:25.353 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Tel Aviv, Shlomo was given a bed at the immigrants’
hostel on HaAliyah Street.

41
00:03:25.683 --> 00:03:29.358 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
After two days the immigrants were free to leave, and each
went their own way.

42
00:03:29.618 --> 00:03:34.195 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo went to Petah Tikva, where a relative of his lived.

43
00:03:34.565 --> 00:03:38.308 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo stayed in Petah Tikva and found work there.

44
00:03:38.608 --> 00:03:42.330 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
From Petah Tikva, Shlomo moved to Rehovot.

45
00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:46.503 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In Rehovot, Shlomo and Zechariah (Keha) Teri bought a plot
together, half each.

46
00:03:46.633 --> 00:03:50.585 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo recalled a sum of 40 pounds (about 16,000 shekels
today, in the family’s estimate).

47
00:03:50.785 --> 00:03:55.198 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo built his home in Rehovot with his own hands.

48
00:03:56.243 --> 00:04:01.348 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Later Shlomo met Yona Nakash. He married her in 1938.

49
00:04:01.638 --> 00:04:04.028 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
In 1938, Yona Nakash and Shlomo Keha married.

50
00:04:04.078 --> 00:04:06.735 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Yona was 17–18 and Shlomo was 30–31.

51
00:04:07.075 --> 00:04:10.635 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Four years later, in 1942, the family posed for this
photograph.

52
00:04:10.705 --> 00:04:13.485 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Shlomo is 34–35 and Yona is 21.

53
00:04:13.565 --> 00:04:16.902 line:80% position:50% align:center size:92%
Ruti is 2–3 and Elisheva is under one year old.
